# Reusability Across Components

Fetching data with loading/error states is repetitive. A **composable** like `useFetch` can encapsulate the logic and be used anywhere.

```javascript
// composables/useFetch.js
import { ref } from 'vue'

export function useFetch(url) {
  const data = ref(null)
  const loading = ref(false)
  const error = ref(null)

  const fetchData = async () => {
    loading.value = true
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url)
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.statusText)
      data.value = await res.json()
    } catch (err) {
      error.value = err.message
    } finally {
      loading.value = false
    }
  }

  fetchData() // auto-fetch on creation

  return { data, loading, error, refetch: fetchData }
}
```

# In a Component

```javascript
import { useFetch } from './composables/useFetch'

export default {
  setup() {
    const { data, loading, error } = useFetch('https://api.example.com/users')
    return { data, loading, error }
  }
}
```

Now you can reuse the same fetching logic across components without duplicating code.
